Chapter: RealModeFields

 A constructor whose payload is moded Reals, returned from `opening`, which
 is the second of the two walks that matched `RealTy` alone.

 `emit-opening-print-field` had the same gap as the result walk and a worse
 failure: its tail is `otherwise -> emit-inline-itoa-and-print`, so a field
 that was not the default Real did not print nothing -- it printed its BIT
 PATTERN through the integer path. A plausible number, in the right place,
 with nothing to say it was wrong.

 The f32 field is the one that needs the width convert. `__real_to_text`
 reads sixty-four bits, so a single handed to it straight is read as a
 double and renders as a number nobody computed.

 IT HAS TO BE A CONSTRUCTOR RATHER THAN A RECORD. `emit-opening-result-print`
 has no `RecordTy` arm at all, so an `opening` returning a record falls to
 the same silent tail and prints nothing whatever its fields are -- measured,
 after this test was first written with a record and produced no output. The
 field walk is reached from the sum printer, so a sum is what reaches it.

Section: Shape

  Sample =
   | Vals (Real) (Real approximate) (Real trapping) (Real saturating)

Section: Entry

  opening : Sample
  opening = Vals 1.5 (to-real-approx 2.5) (to-real-trapping 3.5) (to-real-saturating 4.5)
